                        The only heading in this document                                                               
                        ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━                        
                                                                                                                        
                        A document whose sole heading is its level-one title, and whose body is                         
                        plain prose. This is the shape a README, a changelog entry or a man page                        
                        has, and it is the shape a title-banner feature has to look right in.                           
                                                                                                                        
                        There is no second heading anywhere below, so the table of contents has                         
                        exactly one entry and the banner, if there is one, has nothing to                               
                        compete with.                                                                                   
                                                                                                                        
                        A second paragraph, so the title is followed by more than a single line                         
                        and the spacing beneath it can be judged.
